Package: didml
Title: Difference-in-Differences and LATE with Machine Learning
Version: 0.4.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Andres", "Mena", email = "andres_mena@brown.edu",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = ""))
  )
Description: Unified estimation for difference-in-differences designs with
    machine learning nuisance estimation. Supports sharp DID (Sant'Anna and
    Zhao 2020 via DRDID, and DML-DID of Chang 2020), fuzzy DID (DML-Wald and
    DML-TC of Mena 2026), and an extensible interface for future multi-period
    designs. Cross-fitted nuisance estimation can use Lasso, Random Forest,
    neural networks, OLS, or user-supplied learners. The package includes
    propensity score trimming, clustered standard errors, and a bundled INPRES
    school construction application.
